---
/*
  Sprint 1H shared shell for the golden master's bottom-of-document chrome
  (source/Newsstand - Full Site.dc.html, the `dispatchMode` strip at
  ~lines 621-629 and the publication footer at ~lines 640-644). Both bands
  sit outside every page's `sc-if` conditional in the immutable source, so
  they are genuinely site-wide rather than Cover-specific.

  Post-Sprint-2 fix: the source rotates `dispatchNow` through a five-message
  array on a 4800ms timer, fading each new message in (`animation:dv-fade
  .5s ease both`, ~line 928 of the source's runtime). That rotation is now
  implemented by src/scripts/interactions/dispatch-rotation.ts — the first
  genuinely site-wide interaction module (every other module pathname-gates
  to specific routes; this one runs on every page, matching this band's own
  site-wide placement). The five messages it rotates through are the
  source's own verbatim array; see that file for the full list. This
  paragraph's first message (index 0) is what every page's static HTML
  and visual baseline already show — the module advances from there.

  The dot's continuous slow pulse (`.newsstand-dispatch__dot`) is a
  project-owner-approved addition beyond the golden master itself — the
  source's dot is static with no animation. See DESIGN_DEVIATIONS.md.

  Post-Sprint-2 fix: the publication footer's middle "Set in Archivo
  Black, Barlow Condensed & Source Serif" credit line (source, ~line 643)
  is removed at the project owner's explicit request. The remaining two
  spans (issue/printed-in-Cebu line, copyright line) keep the same
  `justify-content:space-between` treatment, now simply anchored to
  opposite ends of the row.
*/
---

<footer class="newsstand-bottom-chrome">
  <div class="newsstand-dispatch">
    <div class="newsstand-dispatch__inner container">
      <span class="newsstand-dispatch__label">Dispatch</span>
      <span class="newsstand-dispatch__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <p class="newsstand-dispatch__message" data-dispatch-message>
        Case file: teaching a bot to say &ldquo;I don&rsquo;t know&rdquo;
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="newsstand-publication">
    <div class="newsstand-publication__inner container">
      <span>Caballero! Issue 05 &middot; printed in Cebu</span>
      <span>&copy; 2026 John Vincent Caballero</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>

<style>
  .newsstand-bottom-chrome {
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  .newsstand-dispatch {
    background: var(--color-ink);
    color: var(--color-surface);
    border-top: var(--border-width-standard) var(--border-style-solid)
      var(--color-ink);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .newsstand-dispatch__inner {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(10px, 2.5vw, 18px);
    min-height: var(--space-20);
    padding-block: var(--space-11);
  }

  .newsstand-dispatch__label {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    font-size: var(--font-size-mono-10);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-kicker);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-highlight);
  }

  .newsstand-dispatch__dot {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 5px;
    height: 5px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-circle);
    background: var(--color-accent);
    animation: newsstand-dispatch-dot-pulse 2.4s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  /* Slow, continuous "live" pulse — a project-owner-approved addition
     beyond the golden master's static dot. Symmetric (1 -> 0.25 -> 1) and
     declares no competing base opacity, so a single reduced-motion
     iteration (global.css forces animation-iteration-count:1) settles
     back at the initial value of 1 — fully visible, matching every
     existing visual baseline. */
  @keyframes newsstand-dispatch-dot-pulse {
    0%,
    100% {
      opacity: 1;
    }

    50% {
      opacity: 0.25;
    }
  }

  .newsstand-dispatch__message {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    min-width: 0;
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    font-size: clamp(9.5px, 2.1vw, 11px);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    white-space: nowrap;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
  }

  /* The fade only ever applies while dispatch-rotation.ts is actively
     toggling this class for a message change — deliberately NOT an
     unconditional animation on the base rule. The very first paint is
     static server-rendered HTML with no entrance animation: applying one
     unconditionally here would leave every page's opacity in an
     indeterminate, timing-dependent state right as an automated
     screenshot tool disables/freezes animations, which is exactly what
     broke every existing visual baseline by a handful of antialiased
     pixels when this was tried. */
  .newsstand-dispatch__message--rotating {
    animation: newsstand-dispatch-fade var(--duration-scrawl-fade)
      var(--ease-standard) both;
  }

  @keyframes newsstand-dispatch-fade {
    from {
      opacity: 0;
    }

    to {
      opacity: 1;
    }
  }

  .newsstand-publication {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border-top: var(--border-width-standard) var(--border-style-solid)
      var(--color-ink);
  }

  .newsstand-publication__inner {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-8) var(--space-20);
    padding-block: var(--space-18);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    font-size: clamp(9px, 1.8vw, 10px);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-muted-metadata);
  }
</style>
